{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1201425-question-about-mastigos-use-of-magic","id":1201425,"title":"Question About Mastigos Use Of Magic.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-30T15:05:31-07:00","id":1201425,"title":"Question About Mastigos Use Of Magic.","content":"Hello everyone. Quick question,i was re-reading Mage2e. And i just read this quotes in the Mastigos Write Up<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Meditative Mastigos<br /> approach with a still mind, hoping to coax<br /> bodhisattvas out of fanged, skull-bearing gods. </div> </div> </div>What does that mean? I know a bodhisattvas is a buddhist luminary who is trying to elighten people and in back in Mage 1E it was also a group of archmasters trying to enlighten others too. But who are the skull-bearing gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T15:15:02-07:00","id":1201430,"title":"","content":"Goetia, most likely. Or perhaps supernal beings. I could be mistaken, but I believe the point is that Mastigos mages recognize and know the darkness within their own hearts and minds. Knowing that such things have power, they work to use the knowledge and power of that darkness to further themselves. It mostly seems like a description of taking power over one's own oneiros and the beings within.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T15:17:26-07:00","id":1201431,"title":"","content":"The idea is that those Mastigos prefer to approach violent beings [skull-bearing gods] calmly so as to bring out their best, enlighten them, that is, to make them bodhisattvas.<br /> <br /> This kind of Mastigos won't battle fire with fire, rather, he will act through deep understanding and, why not, empathy, towards his enemies, transforming them from the inside into better beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T15:18:04-07:00","id":1201432,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it\u2019s poetic word for \u201ctrying to turn demons into protectors,\u201d I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T15:23:05-07:00","id":1201434,"title":"","content":"ooh that males sense. thanks guys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T15:24:29-07:00","id":1201435,"title":"","content":"It's a metaphor, likely invoking the fierce deities or so-called &quot;wrathful&quot; manifestations of the buddhas. It's about how the Mastigos face hardship, symbolized by inner and supernal demons, and identify the purifying value to be found in that hardship. They wander into dark places and make the darkness theirs, because they understand the darkness was always theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T15:36:02-07:00","id":1201441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1201425-question-about-mastigos-use-of-magic?p=1201435#post1201435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a metaphor, likely invoking the fierce deities or so-called &quot;wrathful&quot; manifestations of the buddhas. It's about how the Mastigos face hardship, symbolized by inner and supernal demons, and identify the purifying value to be found in that hardship. They wander into dark places and make the darkness theirs, because they understand the darkness was always theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>i think i'm getting it now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T15:44:13-07:00","id":1201446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1201425-question-about-mastigos-use-of-magic?p=1201431#post1201431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea is that those Mastigos prefer to approach violent beings [skull-bearing gods] calmly so as to bring out their best, enlighten them, that is, to make them bodhisattvas.<br /> <br /> This kind of Mastigos won't battle fire with fire, rather, he will act through deep understanding and, why not, empathy, towards his enemies, transforming them from the inside into better beings.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1201425-question-about-mastigos-use-of-magic?p=1201435#post1201435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a metaphor, likely invoking the fierce deities or so-called &amp;quot;wrathful&amp;quot; manifestations of the buddhas. It's about how the Mastigos face hardship, symbolized by inner and supernal demons, and identify the purifying value to be found in that hardship. They wander into dark places and make the darkness theirs, because they understand the darkness was always theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This and this. Mastigos may have some of the most terrifying imagery associated with them, but they are in many ways the most understanding and positive of the Paths. Hence my annoyance when they get typecast as something as banal as a hedonists who gets what they want through mind control and demonic possession. (Tome of the Watchtowers, I'm looking at you.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T06:05:41-07:00","id":1201593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1201425-question-about-mastigos-use-of-magic?p=1201446#post1201446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> This and this. Mastigos may have some of the most terrifying imagery associated with them, but they are in many ways the most understanding and positive of the Paths. Hence my annoyance when they get typecast as something as banal as a hedonists who gets what they want through mind control and demonic possession. (Tome of the Watchtowers, I'm looking at you.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately they also are capable of falling prey to the darkness as well. It's not for no reason that Mastigos have the Devil as one of their Tarot cards.<br /> <br /> &quot;The tempter, the slave-master and, perhaps, a bringer of enlightenment through pain and suffering, but most often, he represents bondage. Also, power or intelligence applied to self-ish or base ends. The Mastigos Path claims the Devil as its primary card, interpreting it as the temptation that all of them face, the quick and easy path to power available to any mage versed in Mind magic.<br /> Reversed: Slavery ends; chains break.The Devil Reversed is often a good sign, but can herald unbridled chaos. It can also mean that those enslaved change their focus to loftier goals without los-<br /> ing all fetters.&quot;<br /> <br /> Granted, Mage the Awakening Tarot was a first edition book, but since the second edition core rule book still has Mastigos claiming the card as their own I would say it still applies.<br /> <br /> So yeah. Mastigos see the darkness and often are at the front lines fighting against it, but they're also the ones tempted with some of the darkest stuff out there. Banal? Probably not in the vast majority of cases. Dark? You better believe it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4621_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4621\" data-vbnamecard=\"4621\">Nicolas Milioni</a> As a second answer to your question, I would point back to the 2ed Core rule book on the first page dealing with the Mastigos path:<br /> &quot;You walk through a Warlock\u2019s world with slow steps, while she dances shortcuts through the rattling maze of Pandemonium, guided by gods conjured from her soul.&quot;<br /> <br /> That right there is pretty clearly talking about either goetia or supernal demons, and honestly I always saw that and the part that you quoted as being directly related to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}